answer_generation:  Necessary information: Heredity plays a significant role in obesity, as evidenced by the increased risk of obesity in children of obese parents compared to children of non-obese parents. Studies of adopted twins show that they tend to have the BMI of their biological parents, not their adoptive parents, indicating a genetic component. It is estimated that 25% to 70% of the difference in weight between individuals is due to heredity. Additionally, there is a genetic locus associated with severe obesity, and heredity influences susceptibility to obesity, although environmental and behavioral factors also play a role.

