answer_generation:  Necessary information: The levee is continuous along the left bank (facing downstream) of the Mississippi River from Fayville, Illinois, to past the apex of Dogtooth Island bend. The levee was designed to deflect high velocity floodwaters of the Mississippi River away from agricultural land at the upstream part of the bend. The downstream part of Dogtooth Island bend is not protected by a levee, so low-velocity back flooding has occurred in the area south of the Miller City Road during many floods.

